Z||000016||Songman||06-19-2001||06:32 PM||||I was just funnin ya! It is nice to know that there are still places to go and get a real dealer. Personally, I won't even go into a casino that doesn't have real dealers at the tables. I don't gamble against computers because I know them too well. At least with a real dealer I do have a bit of a chance....<P>I have a lady friend who is a blackjack dealer out in Cripple Creek, CO. Blackjack is my game too... I am not a high roller, but I have learned, for me anyway, if I can stand on at least 14 or 15, that I will generally come out ahead at the end of the day. I used to always go for 19 or 20...<P>I like what you said and I had never thought of it quite that way... "get paid to win"... pretty cool!<P>Anyway, we are glad to have you amongst us.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
